Insights: f(N)=min_{k|N} (lcm_min(k)/k)·N, where lcm_min(k) is the smallest lcm of three distinct numbers summing to k. Ratio r(k)=lcm_min(k)/k is independent of N. Since 2025! is divisible by all k≤2025, g(c)=r(k_min) where k_min is the divisor of N giving smallest r(k). Compute r(k) for k≤2000 (global minima: 6/11, 4/7, 16/25, 30/47, 64/97, 110/167,…). For each N=M+c (M=3^{2025!}) find its small divisors:  
c=0 →k=9, r=2/3;  
c=4M →N=5M, k=9, r=2/3;  
c=1848374 →k=25, r=16/25;  
c=10162574 →k=47, r=30/47;  
c=265710644 →k=97, r=64/97;  
c=44636594 →k=167, r=110/167.  
Sum = 2/3+2/3+16/25+30/47+64/97+110/167 = 224414944/57101475.  
p+q mod 99991 = 41754.
